2
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:22,780
<i>This is a tale from long ago.</i>

3
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:24,380
<i>Benedict Franklin,</i>

4
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:26,150
<i>Mirko Tesla,</i>

5
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:28,260
<i>and Yashima Ryuzo…</i>

6
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:33,010
<i>The geniuses of electricity
had all died young.</i>

7
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:33,030
Kyoto, 36th Year of the Meiji Era

8
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:33,030
Kyoto, 36th Year of the Meiji Era

9
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:37,650
<i>But steam technology advanced
at an astonishing rate worldwide.</i>

10
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:39,460
<i>This is a story from the Meiji Era.</i>

11
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:44,270
The 20th Century
 Electrical
 Catalog

12
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:46,150
The 20th Century
 Electrical
 Catalog

13
00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:52,060
Hey, Kihachi.

14
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:54,050
What now, Big Brother Seiroku?

15
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:55,430
Don't give me that.

16
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,320
You just copied everything I said.

17
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,440
I want you to think up your own bold ideas
worthy of the 20th century.

18
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:06,760
Write about things
that will lead to the Age of Electricity.

19
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:11,680
I can't think of anything. Just saying
"the Age of Electricity" doesn't help.

20
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,130
You can do it.

21
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:15,470
Believe in yourself, Kihachi!

22
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:15,780
What are you doing?!

23
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:17,410
Observe the world around you!

24
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:19,120
Then something will come to you!

25
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,580
It'll help you get over
being such a scaredy-cat too!

26
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,400
Put me down!

27
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:31,280
The 5th National Industrial 
Technology Exhibition

28
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:31,280
The 5th National Industrial 
Technology Exhibition

29
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:42,440
What's the big deal
about turning on some lights?

30
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:45,030
It's a big deal if Seiroku says so.

31
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:46,750
Probably.

32
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:49,150
This is amazing, Big Brother Seiroku.

33
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:51,420
So many different machines!

34
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:54,030
But they're all just steam inventions.

35
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:56,300
Even with this many people, this elevator…

36
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:01,580
Kihachi, wait here.

37
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:02,580
What?

38
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:05,540
I'll be right back.
Try not to be a scaredy-cat.

39
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:07,920
Wait, Big Brother Seiroku!

40
00:02:17,890 --> 00:02:19,100
I don't want to.

41
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:23,610
Damn it!

42
00:02:23,610 --> 00:02:25,350
Be careful!

43
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:27,150
Hey, wait!

44
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:32,150
Hey!

45
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:43,970
Sorry, Seiroku.

46
00:02:43,970 --> 00:02:45,330
It's going to work.

47
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:46,800
Trust me.

48
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:50,830
We're lighting it!

49
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:51,900
Yes, sir!

50
00:03:21,950 --> 00:03:23,330
It's amazing.

51
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:24,230
Yeah.

52
00:03:25,110 --> 00:03:27,190
It's wonderful!

53
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,170
There they are! It's them!

54
00:03:30,170 --> 00:03:32,420
You bastards, what are you doing?

55
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,960
This is bad! You go ahead. I'll catch up!

56
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:47,480
Kihachi, this is the 20th century!
The power of electricity!

57
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,880
Electricity…

58
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:51,950
Its current is still faint,

59
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:54,760
but with the 20th Century Electrical Catalog,

60
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:58,640
we'll create
the Age of Electricity together!

61
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:01,910
Let's do it, Big Brother Seiroku!

62
00:05:25,490 --> 00:05:31,940
Sparks of Tomorrow

63
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:31,940
Chapter One: The Electric Boy

64
00:05:35,650 --> 00:05:39,650
Kyoto, 40th Year of the Meiji Era

65
00:05:35,650 --> 00:05:39,650
Kyoto, 40th Year of the Meiji Era

66
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:41,400
Get your steamed buns!

67
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,030
They're going to vanish like steam!

68
00:05:47,010 --> 00:05:48,310
Behold!

69
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:51,040
Rare steam-engine toys.

70
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:51,930
Is that so?

71
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:56,690
They're made by the best store in Kyoto,
Mizoe Firm, and they're quite valuable.

72
00:05:56,690 --> 00:06:00,260
Come on. You're not a coward.

73
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:59,540
It's your lucky day.

74
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:02,210
Something for the grandchildren?

75
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:03,380
Well…

76
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:04,720
You don't fool me!

77
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:05,340
What?!

78
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:08,530
It's very difficult
to make small steam engines.

79
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:10,040
What are you doing, brat?

80
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:10,950
See? Look!

81
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:12,940
Nothing but springs and hot water!

82
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:15,830
So you were lying! Weren't you?

83
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:18,050
Stop making such a fuss!

84
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:20,220
What a liar.

85
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:25,030
<i>Four years passed.
The Age of Electricity has not arrived.</i>

86
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:28,160
<i>He took the catalog and went to war.</i>

87
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:31,020
<i>He never came back.</i>

88
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:33,600
<i>"We'll create
the Age of Electricity together."</i>

89
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:36,550
<i>He broke that promise.</i>

90
00:06:36,550 --> 00:06:37,920
He fooled me.

91
00:06:39,050 --> 00:06:41,510
We're almost there, Inari!

92
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:58,130
Gracious Deity.

93
00:06:58,130 --> 00:07:00,920
I pick up trash in the city every day.

94
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:03,210
I haven't broken a bowl this week.

95
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:05,680
I try hard not to break my shamisen strings.

96
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,950
I also do as my father tells me.

97
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:09,850
I'll do more good deeds too.

98
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:11,430
My faith is unwavering.

99
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:14,090
I believe in your teachings, Gracious Deity!

100
00:07:14,090 --> 00:07:16,690
So, I humbly ask you.

101
00:07:16,690 --> 00:07:20,840
Please let me talk to my mother in Paradise.

102
00:07:26,150 --> 00:07:28,050
Gods of Takamanohara!

103
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:30,530
Honoring Kamurogi and Kamuromi
as imperial ancestors,

104
00:07:30,530 --> 00:07:37,030
Izanagi performed a purification ritual
at Awakihara, by the inlet of Tachibana…

105
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:38,900
A kagura?

106
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,510
Could it be…

107
00:07:40,510 --> 00:07:42,000
Gracious Deity!

108
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,710
Have you descended to us?

109
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:45,500
Are you here, Gracious Dei…

110
00:07:46,510 --> 00:07:48,320
Hey! Are you okay?

111
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,570
Gracious Deity!

112
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:57,800
Gracious Deity Akubi.

113
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,850
What's wrong with you?

114
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,800
Don't chant prayers at people!

115
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,120
What?

116
00:08:01,650 --> 00:08:03,130
You're not a gracious deity?

117
00:08:03,130 --> 00:08:05,440
Who are you calling a deity?

118
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,150
Quit talking nonsense…

119
00:08:07,150 --> 00:08:09,240
Wait, are you a con artist?

120
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,910
You won't fool me.

121
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:13,670
There is no such thing as deities.

122
00:08:13,670 --> 00:08:16,200
If you doubt the Gracious Deity,
you'll be cursed!

123
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,870
The Gracious Deity is real!

124
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:21,360
Can't you hear the kagura… Wait.

125
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,960
It's stopped?

126
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,000
Don't tell me you…

127
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:34,720
You thought I was a deity because of this?

128
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:37,390
I'm good at believing in stuff.

129
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,850
It's my only talent.

130
00:08:38,850 --> 00:08:40,110
What?

131
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:44,800
I mean, it does sound like a real kagura.

132
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:47,790
What's your name?

133
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:50,150
Huh? My name?

134
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:53,410
Speak into this.

135
00:08:54,830 --> 00:08:59,210
My name is Momokawa Inako.

136
00:08:59,210 --> 00:09:02,380
My family runs
Momokawa Brewery in Fushimi.

137
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:05,670
The school I go to
is the Third Girls' High School…

138
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:07,690
You don't have to say all that.

139
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:16,120
<i>My name is Momokawa Inago.</i>

140
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:19,360
My voice is coming from the machine?

141
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,000
It sounds like "Inago."

142
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Wow! I must be dreaming!

143
00:09:24,650 --> 00:09:25,770
Exactly!

144
00:09:25,770 --> 00:09:28,900
I just recorded your voice
on a new wax cylinder.

145
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:32,360
Your words are engraved into grooves.
It's called "recording."

146
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:35,490
This latest model can record
over two minutes on a single cylinder.

147
00:09:35,490 --> 00:09:38,280
I'm on my way to return—

148
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:39,400
That's enough! Please stop!

149
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:46,130
Here.

150
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:50,670
"We repair machinery
at Horai Buddhist Altar Shop."

151
00:09:50,670 --> 00:09:53,630
"Sakamoto Kihachi"?

152
00:09:53,630 --> 00:09:55,640
Come see me if something breaks down.

153
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:56,910
No, I won't.

154
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,390
Suit yourself, Inago.

155
00:10:00,390 --> 00:10:03,040
It's Inako! No way I'll visit your shop!

156
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:07,940
What a weirdo.

157
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:13,800
Horai Buddhist Altar Shop

158
00:10:24,170 --> 00:10:27,260
Hey, Kihachi. Here's today's repair work.

159
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:28,920
Only two?

160
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,340
Why not find a job that pays better?

161
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:35,870
I can't let a good-for-nothing like you
live here forever for free.

162
00:10:35,870 --> 00:10:39,470
You're not turning down work,
are you, Uncle Bunshichi?

163
00:10:39,470 --> 00:10:41,000
Give it a rest.

164
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,750
I can kick you out whenever I like!

165
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:45,770
I'll finish this in no time.

166
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,860
Mornin', Yajiro.

167
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:49,710
Good morning, Kihachi.

168
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:52,050
Making something today?

169
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:55,320
Well, I don't have much repair work to do.

170
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,700
Maybe I'll make Paradise.

171
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:00,060
Paradise?

172
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:23,910
Setting off.

173
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:31,770
So you like this boy
you met yesterday so much

174
00:11:31,770 --> 00:11:34,870
that your mind went walking during class?

175
00:11:34,870 --> 00:11:36,010
You mean "wandering."

176
00:11:36,010 --> 00:11:38,510
No way. He was such a weirdo.

177
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,930
It's stopping at your house.

178
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:49,130
Konnichiwa

179
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:51,710
Nice to meet you, Momokawa Inako-san.

180
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:53,360
I'm Mizoe Yosuke.

181
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,700
Welcome, Branch Manager.

182
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:00,930
I heard your eldest daughter is engaged.

183
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:03,100
I came by to celebrate.

184
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,730
Goodness.

185
00:12:04,730 --> 00:12:05,910
Thank you.

186
00:12:06,430 --> 00:12:08,080
Noriko, we have a guest!

187
00:12:08,730 --> 00:12:09,900
Welcome to…

188
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:17,110
Congratulations on your engagement.

189
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:20,430
Please, come inside.

190
00:12:24,370 --> 00:12:27,040
Big Sis, is he a guest?

191
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:27,940
Can I help--

192
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:28,870
Inako!

193
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:31,610
You're clumsy. Don't bother coming in.

194
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:34,300
Okay.

195
00:12:37,550 --> 00:12:39,860
What is this?

196
00:12:40,430 --> 00:12:42,220
It's just as it says.

197
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:44,390
According to this contract,

198
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:47,310
the funds I lent you
are to be paid back in full today.

199
00:12:47,310 --> 00:12:48,250
Father!

200
00:12:48,250 --> 00:12:50,460
This is ridiculous.

201
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:53,110
Previously you said
you would wait a full year.

202
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:54,360
Previously?

203
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:57,860
Come now, the contract is right here, isn't it?

204
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:59,840
I can't pay on such short notice!

205
00:13:01,410 --> 00:13:05,960
To think a distinguished family
like Momokawa can't keep a promise.

206
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,790
How regrettable.

207
00:13:07,790 --> 00:13:09,350
I suppose it can't be helped.

208
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:14,090
With the current state
of Momokawa Sake Brewery's finances…

209
00:13:14,090 --> 00:13:15,110
So…

210
00:13:15,110 --> 00:13:19,740
The truth is,
I have a proposal for you, Momokawa-san.

211
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:20,990
A proposal?

212
00:13:21,590 --> 00:13:22,510
Yes.

213
00:13:23,510 --> 00:13:24,870
The Mizoe Firm?

214
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:29,930
They're the number one <i>zaibatsu</i>
in the steam engine industry.

215
00:13:29,930 --> 00:13:34,400
That man is Mizoe Yosuke-sama,
heir to the Mizoe Firm.

216
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,190
It's boiling!

217
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:37,500
It's hot!

218
00:13:41,650 --> 00:13:44,740
Inako-san, if you carry on like that,

219
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:48,220
you won't become a fine person
like your mother.

220
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,370
I'm sorry.

221
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:52,560
What? A marriage?

222
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:56,070
Between my Inako and you, Mizoe Yosuke-sama?

223
00:13:57,130 --> 00:14:00,380
You'd… go so far as to…

224
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:03,010
If you give me a favorable response,

225
00:14:03,010 --> 00:14:06,330
I can be lenient with your debt, Momokawa-san.

226
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:10,080
A good deal for both of us,
don't you think?

227
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,020
I accept.

228
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:20,280
Father!

229
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,110
That's great!

230
00:14:22,110 --> 00:14:23,450
Most pleasing.

231
00:14:23,450 --> 00:14:25,610
Now we're family.

232
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,620
What are you doing?

233
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:27,550
Please excuse us.

234
00:14:27,550 --> 00:14:29,160
What? "Excuse you"?

235
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:30,620
Don't mind me.

236
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:33,540
I'm simply doing as I please in my own house.

237
00:14:43,610 --> 00:14:45,320
Inako! What are you doing?

238
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,530
I thought I'd get the cooling machine out.

239
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:51,410
I'm sorry. I broke it.

240
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:55,040
But I might know someone who can fix it.

241
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:57,270
He has chestnut hair…

242
00:14:57,270 --> 00:15:00,670
It said "Sakamoto Kihachi-san" on his flyer.

243
00:15:01,730 --> 00:15:04,450
But he was a bit weird,
so maybe it's a bad idea.

244
00:15:04,450 --> 00:15:06,620
Sakamoto Kihachi-san?

245
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:06,890
Huh?

246
00:15:06,890 --> 00:15:09,350
Inako, please, go to him now.

247
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:11,010
What? Now?

248
00:15:11,010 --> 00:15:14,000
Yes, right now. And take this.

249
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,020
A letter box?

250
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:17,350
Give this to Sakamoto-san!

251
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:20,090
"Electrical… Catalog"?

252
00:15:20,090 --> 00:15:22,000
Big Sis, do you know him?

253
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:22,990
Please, Inako!

254
00:15:23,510 --> 00:15:25,260
It's very important.

255
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,990
You have to deliver it!

256
