345
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:15,950
We repair 
machinery here.
 Please feel free
 to let yourself
 into the
 storehouse
 at the back.

346
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:15,950
-Sakamoto Kihachi

347
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,950
I wonder if it's okay to go in.

348
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,460
Hello?

349
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:38,480
Yajiro.

350
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,750
Did you finish painting Paradise?

351
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:42,000
Almost.

352
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,170
Excuse me!

353
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:45,730
A customer?

354
00:16:46,670 --> 00:16:48,900
There's a knack to coming in this way.

355
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:51,680
It's that girl?

356
00:16:53,510 --> 00:16:55,990
Please, wait!

357
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:59,060
It's awfully noisy today.

358
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:01,480
Please give me a rag.

359
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:02,520
Yes, ma'am.

360
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:06,510
What are you trying to do?
Please stop this nonsense!

361
00:17:06,510 --> 00:17:08,820
It's not here?

362
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:23,580
Just when I thought I might not see you,
here you are tidying up.

363
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:25,150
May I take a look?

364
00:17:25,150 --> 00:17:28,030
Get away from Noriko-san!

365
00:17:30,510 --> 00:17:31,780
I don't need your help.

366
00:17:32,590 --> 00:17:34,550
That's Noriko-sama for you.

367
00:17:34,550 --> 00:17:36,770
Oh, Yosuke?

368
00:17:36,770 --> 00:17:39,390
He's my eldest daughter's fiancé.

369
00:17:39,390 --> 00:17:41,570
Kuga Kengo, I presume.

370
00:17:41,570 --> 00:17:43,500
You know each other?

371
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:48,010
Hey! Where is the Electrical Catalog?

372
00:17:48,530 --> 00:17:50,010
Electrical Catalog?

373
00:17:50,010 --> 00:17:51,450
Electrical…

374
00:17:51,450 --> 00:17:52,780
Yosuke,

375
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:57,890
the young lady of the house
who just went out had it with her.

376
00:18:00,770 --> 00:18:04,100
We Repair

377
00:18:00,770 --> 00:18:04,100
Machinery

378
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:04,120
I'm about done, but

379
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:05,880
she's still asleep.

380
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:06,860
Leave her be.

381
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:09,130
Let's get started.

382
00:18:09,130 --> 00:18:10,070
Okay.

383
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,390
Where am I?

384
00:18:18,010 --> 00:18:19,620
I can't see.

385
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:22,520
I came to get
the cooling machine repaired,

386
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:26,310
and then I was crushed by something.

387
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:35,610
I must have died.

388
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:38,960
Then this place is…

389
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:42,080
Could it be hell?

390
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,410
Oh, no.

391
00:18:46,210 --> 00:18:51,110
I was always causing trouble
for my father and my sister.

392
00:18:51,110 --> 00:18:53,860
Someone clumsy like me
could never get into Paradise.

393
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:57,090
If I was going to die anyway,

394
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:59,600
I wish I could have seen my mother.

395
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:07,350
Huh? What was that?

396
00:19:31,270 --> 00:19:32,750
She's praying.

397
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:35,280
Talk about excessive devotion.

398
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:38,890
This place…

399
00:19:39,890 --> 00:19:42,810
I've reached Paradise.

400
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:45,980
Mother.

401
00:19:51,650 --> 00:19:53,880
Watch out! Get out of the way!

402
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:02,200
You did it!

403
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:02,200
Incredible!

404
00:20:32,930 --> 00:20:34,000
It's so dark!

405
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:34,920
Mother?!

406
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,930
What's going on? Sakamoto-san?

407
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:46,160
Sakamoto-san, are you from Paradise?

408
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:48,310
First I'm a deity,
and now I'm from Paradise?!

409
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:50,750
You really do believe anything.

410
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:54,630
I died earlier!

411
00:20:54,630 --> 00:20:57,420
And there was a Buddha over there… Huh?

412
00:20:58,130 --> 00:20:59,630
It was a slideshow.

413
00:20:59,630 --> 00:21:00,760
A slideshow?

414
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,490
Horai Buddhist Altar Shop

415
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:08,430
So this is a slide projector?

416
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:13,310
Wow! It's so small but so intricate!

417
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:14,820
Did you draw it?

418
00:21:14,820 --> 00:21:15,900
Huh?

419
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:17,480
What's your name?

420
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:19,150
That's Yajiro Yagura.

421
00:21:19,150 --> 00:21:20,880
He's the son of this house.

422
00:21:21,490 --> 00:21:24,540
And I'm a freeloader
at this Buddhist altar shop.

423
00:21:24,540 --> 00:21:28,520
How did you light up the slide projector
without any gas?

424
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:32,040
It's electricity.

425
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:34,540
See the wire connected to the light bulbs?

426
00:21:34,540 --> 00:21:36,840
If you run electricity
from a generator through it,

427
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:38,920
the filament creates
electrical resistance,

428
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,630
which generates heat and light.

429
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:42,050
The projector uses the light

430
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:44,760
to project the picture
drawn on the cellophane!

431
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,930
This is the first time
I've seen light like this!

432
00:21:50,930 --> 00:21:53,250
It's the century's greatest invention!

433
00:21:53,250 --> 00:21:54,690
The century's…

434
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:58,980
<i>This is the 20th century!
The power of electricity!</i>

435
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:04,780
Filaments made of paper burn out quickly,

436
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:07,430
so the light bulb's light
doesn't last long.

437
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:09,560
This is just child's play.

438
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:12,250
It's not the invention of the century.

439
00:22:12,250 --> 00:22:13,580
That's not true.

440
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:17,960
That slide projector
really made me think I was in Paradise!

441
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:21,070
I was so happy I got to see my mother!

442
00:22:23,840 --> 00:22:25,090
You won't fool me.

443
00:22:25,090 --> 00:22:26,800
I'm not fooling you.

444
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:29,180
You have a talent
for electricity, Sakamoto-san.

445
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:30,410
I believe that!

446
00:22:30,930 --> 00:22:33,230
What's with you?

447
00:22:33,230 --> 00:22:35,880
You believe in people
you don't know a thing about!

448
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:38,920
My talent is believing!

449
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:42,690
Is that even a talent?

450
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:46,450
Everyone just throws their words around.

451
00:22:46,450 --> 00:22:49,620
He didn't even come back with the catalog.

452
00:22:49,620 --> 00:22:51,640
Catalog… Wait!

453
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:53,480
What now?

454
00:22:57,580 --> 00:23:01,880
My older sister
told me to give this to you.

455
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:04,140
What? Your older sister?

456
00:23:04,140 --> 00:23:05,590
What's inside?

457
00:23:05,590 --> 00:23:10,620
Well, if I remember right,
it said "Electrical Catalog" on it.

458
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:12,640
"Electrical Catalog"?

459
00:23:17,130 --> 00:23:19,820
Impossible. That can't be right.

460
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:22,650
It must be some kind of mistake.

461
00:23:22,650 --> 00:23:24,950
There's no way
it could've been at her house…

